@author "Claude (Anthropic)"

; A fold placed under a flap takes the layers between its depth and that
; flap, also where no hinge joins them. The strip is folded in half and in
; half again, so four layers lie over its right quarter. Right of --t the
; two lower layers end in raw edges, and no hinge joins them there: each is
; hinged at its left end to one of the two upper layers. `up to .b` names
; the lowest layer, `under .u` the third. The second layer lies above the
; first and below the third, so it folds with the first; the third and
; fourth stay.

paper rectangle 2 1

.h = free on --ab from .a at 1/2            ; (1, 0): the first fold's hinge
.e = free on --da from .a at 1/2            ; (0, 1/2)
.p = free on --ab from .a at 3/4            ; (3/2, 0)
.q = free on --cd from .c at 1/4            ; (3/2, 1)
.r = free on --ab from .a at 7/8            ; (7/4, 0) on the lowest layer
.s = free on --cd from .c at 1/8            ; (7/4, 1) on the lowest layer
.u = free on --ab from .a at 3/8            ; (3/4, 0): on the third layer
fold (map .a onto .b)                       ; left half over, raw edges at the right
fold (through .p .q) (moving .h)            ; left half of the stack over again
fold (through .r .s) (moving .b) (up to .b) (under .u) as --t

--cut = (perp --t through .e)

; assert steps = 3
; assert faces = 6
; assert .b = (3/2, 0)
; assert .a = (3/2, 0)
; assert .c = (3/2, 1)
; assert .u = (7/4, 0)
; assert --t is valley
